{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## The gate lost its own PASS — this bug destroyed a 14-minute LLM review\n\nWhile earning the plan-review attestation for THIS ticket, the bug this ticket describes\ndestroyed the review that was reviewing it. Recorded verbatim because it is the cleanest\nin-the-wild instance yet, and it happened to rebar's own gate machinery rather than to a comment.\n\n`rebar review-plan royal-weariless-zebrafish` completed with **`\"verdict\": \"PASS\"`, 0 blocking\nfindings, `\"signable\": true`** after ~14 minutes and 28 LLM calls. Neither the attestation nor\nthe review record survived:\n\n    signature: {'signed': False,\n                'error': 'flock: could not acquire lock after 60s\n                          (holder: host=name-... pid=89059 held=103s pid_state=live)',\n                'event': 'plan_review_generation_retry', 'retryable': True}\n\n    plan review PASSED but the attestation could not be persisted:\n      flock: could not acquire lock after 60s (holder: ... held=103s pid_state=live)\n    run `rebar sign-review 10c3-5a33-2e25-4584` to re-sign from the recorded review (no LLM re-run)\n\nThe offered recovery **did not work**, because the PASS record itself was also lost:\n\n    $ rebar sign-review 10c3-5a33-2e25-4584\n    {\"ok\": false, \"signed\": false, \"verdict\": \"BLOCK\",\n     \"reason\": \"the latest review was not a signable PASS (verdict=BLOCK)\n                — run `rebar review-plan` to produce a fresh verdict\"}\n\nSo **two** writes were discarded by one contention episode: the signature AND the PASS sidecar.\nThe recorded verdict silently remained the PREVIOUS round's BLOCK, which is the worst shape — the\nsystem does not merely lose the result, it retains a stale contradicting one. The full LLM review\nhad to be re-run from scratch.\n\n### Why this is decisive evidence for the chosen remedy\n\n* **The holder was `held=103s`, and 163s on a second sample** — far beyond the 60s budget. The\n  re-measurement above established that writer COUNT no longer exhausts the budget; this shows\n  holder DURATION routinely does, on an ordinary developer host with a handful of agents running.\n  That is exactly the failure mode bounded retry addresses and fair queueing does not.\n* **The retry ceiling would have saved it.** A 103s holder is inside the planned ~181.5s ceiling\n  (3 passes x 60s + backoff), so the attestation write would have landed on pass 2 as latency\n  instead of loss.\n* **`event_append.py:382` is on the failing path** (`signing.py:574 append_event` ->\n  `_seam.py:521 write_and_push` -> `event_append.py:382`) and is one of this change's three opt-in\n  sites. This change therefore fixes this exact occurrence, not an analogue of it.\n\n### Adjacent defect, NOT in this ticket's scope\n\n`sign-review`'s advertised recovery path is only sound when the sidecar persisted but the signature\ndid not. When BOTH are lost to the same contention episode, the guidance printed to the user\n(\"run `rebar sign-review` ... no LLM re-run\") is misleading — it names a recovery that cannot\nwork, and the stale prior BLOCK is what `sign-review` then reports. Filed separately rather than\nfolded in here."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786524181932899001,"uuid":"eff780d9-5c2a-46a9-babf-b2383f2ca6cd"}